TI  - HCICF: A Human Centred Intelligent Conversational Framework integrating Contextual Memory and Explainable AI for Next Generation Human Computer Interaction
AB  - Human-Computer Interaction (HCI) is rapidly evolving with the emergence of Large Language Models (LLMs) and conversational artificial intelligence.However, existing conversational systems still face limitations in maintaining longterm contextual continuity, personalization, explainability, transparency, and user trust.This paper proposes a **Human-Centred Intelligent Conversational Framework (HCICF)** that integrates hierarchical contextual memory, semantic knowledge retrieval, dynamic prompt construction, transformer-based reasoning, Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI), adaptive user modelling, and continuous feedback within a unified architecture.The proposed framework maintains working, episodic, semantic, and preference memory to preserve relevant information across interactions.Dynamic prompt construction combines the current query, retrieved context, user profile, external knowledge, previous decisions, and system constraints to generate context-rich prompts.An explainability pipeline further provides contextual attribution, supporting evidence, reasoning summaries, and confidence estimation, while adaptive learning continuously updates user preferences and contextual knowledge based on feedback and behavioural signals.Experimental evaluation considers contextual consistency, response relevance, explainability, user trust, user satisfaction, and task completion.HCICF achieves 93.2% contextual consistency, 94.6% response relevance, 91.4% explainability, 89.7% user trust, 92.1% user satisfaction, and 94.3% task completion, with an overall average performance of 92.55%, compared with 81.23% for RAG and 74.10% for a conventional LLM.The results demonstrate that integrating persistent contextual memory, explainable reasoning, knowledge retrieval, and adaptive personalization improves the effectiveness, transparency, and reliability of conversational AI for next-generation human-computer interaction.
